Authorization: {{reviewer1}}


### =========================================================================
### 12. SAP_ERROR RETRY FLOW & EDIT ALLOWED
### =========================================================================
### *Note: To test this, the form must have 'generalStatus': 'SAP_ERROR' in the database.
### We use the form from Section 2 (baseFormId) assuming it reached step 4 and failed.

### REVIEWER 4 can EDIT when form has SAP_ERROR (Expected: 200 or 201)
# @name RetryEdit
POST {{baseUrl}}/RequestForm(ID={{baseFormId}},IsActiveEntity=true)/CatalogService.draftEdit
Authorization: {{reviewer4}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "PreserveChanges": true }

### REVIEWER 4 can UPDATE when form has SAP_ERROR (Expected: 200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/RequestForm(ID={{baseFormId}},IsActiveEntity=false)
Authorization: {{reviewer4}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "materialGroupNumber_ProductGroup": "ICT1002" }

### REVIEWER 4 (Last Approver) can APPROVE again to retry (Expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/RequestForm(ID={{baseFormId}},IsActiveEntity=true)/CatalogService.approveRequest
Authorization: {{reviewer4}}


